   "source": [
    "## Converting the Origin Values\n",
    "\n",
    "The origin column uses the numbers 1, 2, and 3. I replaced these numbers with USA, Asia, and Europe to make the data easier to understand.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2dda0a90-b8a2-4d78-af17-3ccd6e719c3f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "b80bcff1-6556-4ef5-a529-dfd42c40b62c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "origin\n",
       "USA       249\n",
       "Europe     79\n",
       "Asia       70\n",
       "Name: count, dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 8,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "cars[\"origin\"] = cars[\"origin\"].replace({\n",
    "    1: \"USA\",\n",
    "    2: \"Asia\",\n",
    "    3: \"Europe\"\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "cars[\"origin\"].value_counts()\n"
   ]
  },
