   "source": [
    "The scatterplot shows a positive relationship between weight and horsepower. In general, heavier cars tend to have more horsepower, although there are some differences between individual cars.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b4d14660-aa35-4c74-aeff-99ba7d7a9b1a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Does Average MPG Differ by Origin?\n",
    "\n",
    "I wanted to see whether cars from different origins have different average miles per gallon.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "5beee9a3-a2d4-42ad-a2b4-bd87f697b79b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "average_mpg = cars.groupby(\"origin\")[\"mpg\"].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "average_mpg.plot(kind=\"bar\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title(\"Average MPG by Origin\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Origin\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Average MPG\")\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b18c4f6-4420-4795-9bfb-5ba9da43c79c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The chart shows that average MPG differs by origin. European cars have the highest average MPG, followed by Asian cars, while cars from the USA have the lowest average MPG in this dataset.\n"
   ]
